   "subject": "Re: integrate data points to plot",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "As plotProbe() just creates a standard plot, you can add point to that \r<br>plot by using the points() function, something like\r<br>\r<br>points(data.AOP$EF, data.AOP$AOP, add = TRUE)\r<br>\r<br>Yves.\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "\r<br>On 06/01/2018 04:15 PM, Daniel Groß wrote:\r<br>&gt; Hello,\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; my question is whether it is possible to integrate and show data points \r<br>&gt; in a graphic which is built out of a lavaan calculated SEM? Below is my code\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; |\r<br>&gt; fit &lt;-sem(HS.model,data =data.AOP,<a href=\"http://std.lv\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://std.lv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792425502081000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1X-xlWSBO7uyR67nrUIzsR\">std.lv</a>=T,estimator =&quot;MLM&quot;)\r<br>&gt; summary(fit,standardized=T,fit.measures=T)\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; # simple slope analysis\r<br>&gt; \r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "&gt; result2wayMC &lt;-probe2WayMC(fit,c(&quot;EF&quot;,&quot;AOP&quot;,&quot;EF.AOP&quot;),\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "&gt; &quot;BSCS&quot;,c(&quot;AOP&quot;),c(-1,1))\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; result2wayMC\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; plotProbe(result2wayMC,xlim=c(-1,1))\r<br>&gt; |\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>"
